{
    "word": "unencumbered",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "50abc118-b0c6-3ba4-9622-404bdd0162c4",
                "word": "unencumbered",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6d46420e-d5db-485e-b162-56016a2bc3b7",
                        "entry_id": "50abc118-b0c6-3ba4-9622-404bdd0162c4",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more unencumbered"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b02bfa24-278c-425e-acf8-b597fd6501fa",
                        "entry_id": "50abc118-b0c6-3ba4-9622-404bdd0162c4",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most unencumbered"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb1ca38a-3933-393a-94cc-450f5888ed7e",
                        "entry_id": "50abc118-b0c6-3ba4-9622-404bdd0162c4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not burdened with worries, cares or responsibilities."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2018b09d-63a7-42c4-a766-f771a39cbc4c",
                                "sense_id": "fb1ca38a-3933-393a-94cc-450f5888ed7e",
                                "text": "This difference operates in favor of socialism, not only because speculation about general principles provides an opportunity for the play of the imagination of those who are unencumbered by much knowledge of the facts of present-day life […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f14c0b13-6a44-30e5-994e-245992ad34dd",
                        "entry_id": "50abc118-b0c6-3ba4-9622-404bdd0162c4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Free of encumbrance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e00fecd2-4bf9-464f-ac64-29cc6cb71e3e",
                                "sense_id": "f14c0b13-6a44-30e5-994e-245992ad34dd",
                                "text": "The commuters from the suburbs come unencumbered with luggage, children and prams, and can almost be relied upon to find their way blindfold to their trains."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ad037be-4c58-4f1f-a98d-d835d530a261",
                                "sense_id": "f14c0b13-6a44-30e5-994e-245992ad34dd",
                                "text": "Now he knew that something more than revenge had prompted Rokoff to pitch him overboard—the Russian had managed to obtain possession of the papers Tarzan had wrested from him at Bou Saada. The ape-man swore softly, and let his coat and shirt sink into the Atlantic. Before many hours he had divested himself of his remaining garments, and was swimming easily and unencumbered toward the east."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "306a6adf-fdf9-4bfc-b3ed-5a3946587511",
                                "sense_id": "f14c0b13-6a44-30e5-994e-245992ad34dd",
                                "text": "That large room had always awed Ivor: even as a child he had never wanted to play in it, for all that it was so limitless, the parquet floor so vast and shiny and unencumbered, the windows so wide and light with the fairy expanse of Kensington Gardens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82fd8e80-54ef-4619-9516-588f58650bc6",
                                "sense_id": "f14c0b13-6a44-30e5-994e-245992ad34dd",
                                "text": "\"For myself, because of the baggage of 30 years of balkanisation, I think the elegant solution is to take operations back into the public sector. It will mean you can have a whole-industry approach to running the railway, unencumbered by contractual differences.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32198cd6-bb1c-37c7-93a8-fc0f1b41cb88",
                        "entry_id": "50abc118-b0c6-3ba4-9622-404bdd0162c4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not subject to any claims."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of property"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d60e01d-894d-46cd-beac-cb6c7e6978b2",
                                "sense_id": "32198cd6-bb1c-37c7-93a8-fc0f1b41cb88",
                                "text": "\"You are wrong,\" replied Mrs. Courtenaye: \"luxury is but a trifle—not so power and position. With an unencumbered estate, you take the first place in the county; you obtain the finest field for the exertion of your talents; and England has no distinction to which you may not reasonably aspire.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "45592868-e6af-480f-9be4-935483b52f53",
                        "source_entry_id": "50abc118-b0c6-3ba4-9622-404bdd0162c4",
